# Release gate: what must be true before acme 2.4.0 ships, and who said so.
# B2-B5 are scripts that re-run on their own: CI every minute, the others
# whenever the files they read change. B6 is a person's call: verify it once
# you've tried the staging build. B7 is release notes an agent drafts and a
# person verifies. C says whether each row passes, ready is all of them, and
# the tag action refuses to run until ready is true.
#
# Two rows fail as shipped: src/acme/__init__.py still says 2.3.1, and
# migration 007 has no down step. Fix either file and its row turns green on
# its own. The same board is a CI gate: `recalc check board.recalctemplate --cell ready`
# exits non-zero until it reads true. tools/ stands in for gh and the tag step.
version = 2.4.0
A1 = Check
B1 = Result
C1 = Passes?
A2 = CI on main
B2 = $ sh tools/gh run list --branch main --limit 1 --json conclusion # every: 60000
C2 = = {B2} == 'success'
A3 = Changelog has a section for the version
B3 = $ grep -c "^## {version}" CHANGELOG.md || true # watch: CHANGELOG.md
C3 = = {B3} > 0
A4 = Version strings agree
B4 = $ sh scripts/versions.sh {version} # watch: {pyproject.toml,src/**}
C4 = = {B4.code} == 0
A5 = Every migration can be rolled back
B5 = $ sh scripts/check-down.sh # watch: migrations/**
C5 = = {B5.code} == 0
A6 = Smoke-tested on staging
B6 = Verify this cell once you've tried the staging build.
C6 = = {B6.mark} == 'verified'
A7 = Release notes
B7 = @claude('Draft the release notes for acme {version}: one sentence on what the release is for, then one line per change a user will notice, from CHANGELOG.md and the pull requests in merged.txt, each naming its PR by number. Leave out dependency bumps unless they fix something a user would see. Plain text, no headings.')
C7 = = {B7.mark} == 'verified'
ready = = and({C2}, {C3}, {C4}, {C5}, {C6}, {C7})
blocking = = countif({C2:C7}, 'false')
tag = ! test {ready} = true || { echo "not ready: {blocking} of the checks fail"; exit 1; }; sh tools/tag {version}
